# Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is a secret — the site has no keys.

# The site's own origin. Two jobs:
#
#  1. Canonicals, sitemap and share-card URLs resolve from it. On Vercel
#     this is unnecessary: VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL supplies it, and
#     previews then correctly avoid claiming to be canonical.
#
#  2. It is the build's FALLBACK DATA SOURCE. If the season compute fails
#     (openf1 rate-limits a burst of ~22 requests fairly readily), the
#     build fetches the last good bundle from this origin instead. Without
#     it the build has nothing to fall back on and REFUSES to continue,
#     rather than baking a data-less page — which is deliberate, but means
#     a throttled openf1 will block a local build until you set this.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://f1-website-three.vercel.app
